  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2-Hexenyl-beta-glucopyranoside and Phosphodiesterase 6C, mediated through intermediate targets. The compound 2-Hexenyl-beta-glucopyranoside is identified as a target of CDK3/cyclin E, which in turn is a target of Methyl 2-(3-Bromo-5-Hydroxy-4-Methoxyphenyl)Acetate, and this latter compound is also a target of Phosphodiesterase 6C. Similarly, 2-Hexenyl-beta-glucopyranoside is linked to Fucosyltransferase 6, which is a target of the same compound that targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings indicate that 2-Hexenyl-beta-glucopyranoside may act as a modulator of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple pathways, possibly by influencing the activity of CDK3/cyclin E or Fucosyltransferase 6. The evidence is consistent across different paths, suggesting a robust connection between the compound and the enzyme, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
